## 210-231 · Closed Round-1 review findings on splice-sanitizer branch (W1/W2/F1/H1-H5)
The coordinator (source-agent-id 379f3cad) delivered the Round-1 review adjudication: two wire-affecting findings, one fidelity finding, five hygiene findings — all sustained or accepted, to be closed on `fix/historian-splice-sanitize`. Budget discipline specified: scoped law files while iterating, batteries once at the very end, no flake chasing.

The findings:
- **W1 (wire)**: `media_placeholder` raw filename at `crates/mc-module/src/historian_chunk.rs:1574` splices `media.filename` into the `[media:{kind} {} {filename}]` chunk line with no fold/defang — a filename with `\n` or `] U:` reproduces the exact splice class this branch closed, and the L5 census never sees it (scanners only match `TC: ` shapes). Fix: route filename through `sanitize_splice_text`. Census extended to cover non-TC content-bearing line producers. TS lane skips media parts entirely — pin that asymmetry with a law.
