#2636: LKG durable slots survive rotation (§12.6): a rotation pass is by construction a bust pass, so the capture refreshes on that same pass; keeping the durable row avoids manufacturing a boot rebuild window between rotation and first capture.
#2637: The persistence READER contract governs cached_m0_bytes reuse: an existing legacy row must be treated as first-render (empty region), never served as region bytes.
#2647: The frozen-region scheme's cache-resiliency imperatives must be structural foundations, not band-aids re-implemented on top — each law is a structural property of the design.
#2657: clearCachedM0M1 is the central invalidation funnel for cached_m0_bytes with nine production call sites (compartment-storage.ts ×5, store-generation-rebase.ts, history-boundary-repair.ts ×2, compartment-runner-recomp.ts, plus Pi compaction-off-pi.ts ×2); all must route through the receipted clear with per-caller reasons — region-blind direct writes to the column are forbidden.
#2661: L0 (owner law, above L1): SINGLE WRITER, SCHEDULE-ONLY — exactly one mechanism (the boundary transaction) may change bytes MC contributes to the served wire; every other subsystem holds no write authority and may only enqueue intent (queue/marker → named boundary → transaction); sole synchronous exception: model-issued stamp intent. Foreign byte-zones (host system region) are outside the contract by design. Enforcement: per-actor producer census; any direct write fails CI.
#2674: The Pi trim path must never derive wire-affecting decisions from region rows unguarded — post Stage P2 the enforced property is: a boundary may drive trimming only when written in the same transaction as the bytes it covers. Fold rotations co-write region bytes + boundary under one BEGIN IMMEDIATE (legitimate); the funnel's direct writers null the boundary at the write site, and the reader refuses unservable (corrupt) regions — not per-caller patches.
#2704: Pi is a frozen-system-region serving lane (Stage P2, design §23): the boot capability isSystemRegionLane (transform_mode pinned "ts") is threaded once per process; serve happens in processSystemPromptForCache (before_agent_start) appending decodeSystemRegionRow bytes after the host bytes with the hash covering host bytes only; materializeM0Pi's regionOptions branch is the second named production caller of executeSystemRegionRotation (first being materializeM0 in inject-compartments.ts); region-lane injection splices no synthetic heads. The Rust module stays non-serving: the lane predicate excludes rust, and the refusal census confines cached_m0_bytes in crates/ to the single_store_repair.rs reset list.
#2717: The pending_growth rotation arm is deleted as redundant: the four DELTA markers (maxMemoryId, maxCompartmentSeq, profileVersion, docs hash) already measure the deltas it was meant to capture; with markers correctly wired, no separate pending-growth trigger is needed.
#2734: PendingOp.operation is the provenance discriminator in pending_ops: `"drop"` indicates an agent-origin ctx_reduce stamp, `"auto_drop"` indicates a system-origin queue row (sweeper, compaction, historian). This field is the sanctioned mechanism for distinguishing revocable from non-revocable rows without a new column.
